                  <msItem>
                     <title>Miscellanea medica</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">It seems likely that the whole MS (pts i--ix)
                        is from Lanercost. Pt ix has the inscription 'Liber ffratris Nich. de
                        Morland ex dono Willelmi de Langedale [s. xiii, xiv] cuius usum proprium
                        idem Nicholaus concessit cessit (sic) domino Iohanni de Buchcaster [i.e.
                        Bewcastle]'. Morland and Langdale are in Westmorland. A John of Bewcastle
                        was prior of Lanercost 1338--54 (Heads of Religious Houses, 2. 403).</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate>s. xii, xiii</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_292">Lanercost, Cumberland.
                        Augustinian priory of St Mary Magdalen. </orgName><p>'Liber sancte Marie
                        Magdalene de Lanrecost si quis inde eum asportauerit anathema sit' at foot
                        of first leaf of pt iii.</p></provenance>
               </history>
